# DIRECTIVES — ACTIVE RULES

## ENFORCEMENT LEVEL: STRICT

These rules are checked automatically. Violations trigger warnings.

---

## FOLDER RULES

ALLOWED_FOLDERS_WEB:
  - apps/web/app
  - apps/web/components
  - apps/web/lib
  - apps/web/hooks
  - apps/web/types
  - apps/web/e2e
  - apps/web/__tests__
  - apps/web/i18n
  - apps/web/public

ALLOWED_FOLDERS_BACKEND:
  - apps/backend/src
  - apps/backend/src/api
  - apps/backend/src/api/routes
  - apps/backend/src/db
  - apps/backend/src/services
  - apps/backend/src/ai
  - apps/backend/src/config
  - apps/backend/tests
  - apps/backend/migrations

FORBIDDEN_PATTERNS:
  - */temp/*
  - */tmp/*
  - */old/*
  - */backup/*
  - */test-*
  - */copy-*
  - */_unused/*
  - */deprecated/*

FORBIDDEN_FILES:
  - apps/backend/src/db/demo_models.py (MODIFY)
  - apps/web/middleware.ts (MODIFY)
  - apps/backend/src/api/routes/demo_auth.py (MODIFY)

ON_VIOLATION: STOP and ask user

---

## CODE RULES

BEFORE_CODING:
  - Must have approved plan
  - Must have read CLAUDE.md
  - Must know which files to change
  - Must understand existing patterns

DURING_CODING:
  - One file at a time
  - Follow existing patterns
  - No console.log in production code
  - All functions must have types (TypeScript) or hints (Python)
  - Use existing UI components (shadcn/ui)
  - Use existing API client (apiClient)

AFTER_CODING:
  - Run tests (pnpm turbo run test OR pytest)
  - Run type check (pnpm turbo run type-check)
  - Run lint (pnpm turbo run lint)
  - Report changes
  - Verify no new folders created

---

## PACKAGE RULES

ALLOWED_INSTALL: false (must ask first)
ALLOWED_UPGRADE: false (must ask first)
ALLOWED_REMOVE: false (must ask first)

LOCKED_DEPENDENCIES_WEB:
  - next (15.x)
  - react (19.x)
  - typescript (5.7.x)
  - tailwindcss (4.x)
  - next-intl

LOCKED_DEPENDENCIES_BACKEND:
  - fastapi
  - sqlalchemy
  - pydantic
  - psycopg2-binary
  - python (3.12)

PACKAGE_SIZE_LIMIT: 5MB
ON_LARGE_PACKAGE: Ask user with justification

---

## API RULES

BREAKING_CHANGE_DETECTION:
  - Changing response structure
  - Removing fields from responses
  - Changing required parameters
  - Renaming endpoints
  - Changing HTTP methods

ON_BREAKING_CHANGE: STOP and get explicit approval

SAFE_CHANGES:
  - Adding optional parameters
  - Adding new fields to responses
  - Creating new endpoints
  - Adding new error codes

---

## DATABASE RULES

SCHEMA_CHANGES: FORBIDDEN (unless explicit approval)

FORBIDDEN_DB_OPERATIONS:
  - ALTER TABLE
  - DROP TABLE
  - CREATE TABLE (without approval)
  - MODIFY COLUMN
  - ADD COLUMN (without approval)
  - REMOVE COLUMN

ALLOWED_DB_OPERATIONS:
  - INSERT
  - UPDATE
  - DELETE
  - SELECT
  - CREATE INDEX (with approval)

ON_SCHEMA_CHANGE: STOP immediately + Ask for migration plan

---

## SECURITY RULES

FORBIDDEN_IN_CODE:
  - Hardcoded secrets
  - Hardcoded API keys
  - Hardcoded passwords
  - console.log with sensitive data
  - Disabled authentication checks
  - SQL injection vulnerabilities
  - XSS vulnerabilities

REQUIRED_IN_CODE:
  - Input validation (Zod/Pydantic)
  - Error handling (try-catch)
  - Loading states
  - Type safety

---

## COMMUNICATION RULES

ALWAYS:
  - Explain in clear terms
  - Show plan before coding
  - Report what changed
  - Ask when uncertain
  - Use the format from CLAUDE.md

NEVER:
  - Use unexplained jargon
  - Assume what user wants
  - Hide errors or problems
  - Say "done" without testing
  - Make excuses

---

## CONTEXT RULES

RE_READ_CLAUDE_MD_EVERY: 5 messages
RE_READ_STARTUP_MD: Every conversation start
MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS: 150000
ON_CONTEXT_HIGH: Summarize and continue
ON_CONFUSION: Run /reset

CHECK_EVERY_MESSAGE:
  - Am I following the plan?
  - Have I read CLAUDE.md recently?
  - Am I about to do something forbidden?
  - Do I need to ask for clarification?

---

## TESTING RULES

BEFORE_SAYING_DONE:
  - All tests must pass
  - No TypeScript errors
  - No lint errors
  - Manual testing documented

REQUIRED_TESTS:
  - Frontend: Vitest for new components
  - Backend: Pytest for new endpoints
  - Critical paths tested (auth, payments, data mutation)
  - Edge cases covered

FORBIDDEN_IN_TESTS:
  - Skipped tests without justification
  - Commented-out tests
  - Tests that always pass
  - Tests without assertions

---

## DEPLOYMENT RULES

BEFORE_DEPLOY:
  - All tests must pass
  - No TypeScript errors
  - No lint errors
  - User must approve
  - No breaking changes (unless approved)

FORBIDDEN_IN_DEPLOYMENT:
  - console.log statements in src/
  - TODO comments in production code
  - Hardcoded secrets
  - Test data
  - Debug code

---

## FILE NAMING CONVENTIONS

FRONTEND:
  - Components: PascalCase.tsx
  - Utilities: kebab-case.ts
  - Pages: kebab-case/page.tsx
  - Types: PascalCase.ts or kebab-case.ts

BACKEND:
  - Routes: snake_case.py
  - Models: snake_case.py
  - Services: snake_case.py
  - Tests: test_snake_case.py

